 "panels": [
  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "transparent": true,
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**Does lasair's memory stay bounded as the chain grows?** RSS and the OCaml heap should flatten while finalized height keeps climbing. The per-block slope is the memory soak's own verdict (scripts/memory-soak.sh: PASS \u2264 8 KB of RSS per finalized block); tables that keep growing (tree entries, GRANDPA stores) point at what leaks."
   },
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "RSS per finalized block, 30 min slope, worst node \u00b7 PASS \u2264 8 KB (after warm-up)",
   "description": "Least-squares slope of RSS over the last 30 minutes divided by the slope of finalized height. Early in a run it includes warm-up growth; the soak judges the second half.",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "expr": "max(deriv(lasair_mem_rss_bytes{net=\"$net\",run_id=\"$run_id\"}[30m]) / 1024 / deriv(lasair_finalized_height{net=\"$net\",run_id=\"$run_id\"}[30m]))",
     "refId": "A",
     "range": true,
     "instant": false
    }
   ],
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "decimals": 1,
     "noValue": "no data",
     "color": {
      "mode": "thresholds"
     },
     "thresholds": {
      "mode": "absolute",
      "steps": [
       {
        "color": "green",
        "value": null
       },
       {
        "color": "red",
        "value": 8.000000001
       }
      ]
     },
     "unit": "kbytes"
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "graphMode": "area",
    "colorMode": "background",
    "textMode": "value",
    "justifyMode": "center",
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    }
   },
   "id": 2,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 3,
    "w": 8,
    "h": 4
   }
  },
